WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:04.259
Well, so a lot of my books are actually multiple books combined into one, right?

00:00:04.259 --> 00:00:08.700
So, for example, Cryptonomicon is a
World War 2 book and a modern-day book

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.929
that are interleaved. And that's true of
a bunch of my books. So this one is a

00:00:12.929 --> 00:00:18.300
high fantasy novel that's embedded in a
techno thriller. And the techno thriller

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:24.330
is about a guy who dies. And it turns out
that when he was a younger guy, he came

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:29.060
into a bunch of money. Was that my beard hitting the the mic?

00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:34.440
Sometimes that happens. When he was a
younger guy and he came into money for

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:39.149
the first time, he signed one of these wills that gives instructions on

00:00:39.149 --> 00:00:44.399
how to preserve his body after he dies.
So he'd be brought back to life. And

00:00:44.399 --> 00:00:47.969
then he forgot about it. Because he
didn't really care; it was just sort of a

00:00:47.969 --> 00:00:55.219
thing he did on a whim. But then he dies
unexpectedly and his family and friends

00:00:55.219 --> 00:01:01.530
find this will sitting there like a time
bomb. And they have to figure out how to

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:06.689
carry out the terms of the will. And
because the deceased is a

00:01:06.689 --> 00:01:10.170
billionaire, they can't claim that
there's a lack of resources, you know?

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:18.330
So he gets scanned. The way they do
it is they scan his brain and then later

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:24.540
on he is brought back to life in the
cloud as a digital simulation of a

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:32.549
consciousness. And there's nothing there. And he wants qualia; he wants something

00:01:32.549 --> 00:01:41.430
to be there. I've just made Alvin very
happy by working in his favorite word.

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:51.299
Your brain is hooked up in such a way that you know it needs

00:01:51.299 --> 00:01:56.700
stimuli, it needs inputs. And he's not getting any of that.

00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:03.750
So he has to create them. And he starts to build a world that he doesn't have clear

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:09.060
coherent memories of where he came from. Just fragmented, jumbled

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:13.530
memories. And so he begins to try to
assemble a coherent world out of that

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:17.849
and ends up building a world that's kind
of like our world, but it's sort of a

00:02:17.849 --> 00:02:21.959
mash-up of our world with, you know, the
Bible and Greek myths and Lord of the

00:02:21.959 --> 00:02:26.459
Rings and, you know, whatever was going
through his head. And then other people

00:02:26.459 --> 00:02:31.470
start showing up and sort of spreading
out and populating this world. And that

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:40.019
is the world in which the high
fantasy novel takes place. And we know

00:02:40.019 --> 00:02:43.950
that it's a digital simulation, but the
people who live there don't know that.

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:49.680
It's as real to them as this world is to
everyone here, raising the question of: is

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:54.350
it just turtles all the way down?

